// Criterion: an `rwfunc` parameter must be a single type; a union leaves callers unable to deduce argument types.
//
// Negative case (4th state): **layout is expected to fail**, and the diagnostic must point to the parameter side.
// If the check were removed, layout would succeed -> FAIL ("expected failure passed");
// if the check only rejected union returns, layout would still fail for the wrong reason -> FAIL as well.
//
// Paired with `types/rwfunc_union_return.kv` (return side) and `lib/rwir_union_kept.kv`
// (`rwir` declarations keep unions) -- without all three, banning unions across all signatures would falsely pass.
//
// Reference: 03-type-system/05-langtype-signature-type-exprs.kv (normative section),
//            05-runtime-semantics/04-function-calls.kv.
// Expected error: rwfunc parameter must be a single type

rwfunc pick(*int64|float64 #x) -> (*int64 #r) {
	0 -> *r
}
